ender_html.clj AND are absent from the done-set, so the tick still offers them as candidates; the stub misleads a human reader but does NOT corrupt pipeline accounting", :separate-case "isic-4730 shipped a different fabricated console naming operators (Akita Fuel Mart, Atlantis Fuels) absent from its seed data"}, :approved-by-defect {:scope "fleet-wide scaffold defect, confirmed independently by 6 agents (isic-2592 2814 2393 4530 3250 + the isic-9522 reference)", :detail "operation :request-approval attaches the approver to the record :payload key, but store/commit-record! destructures :value and never reads :payload, so approval attribution never reaches the SSoT and survives only in the transient run audit", :handling "agents rendered it honestly (isic-2393 prints not-on-record; isic-3250 joins the approver back from :approval-granted audit facts) rather than printing a name the store does not hold", :status "still unfixed at the scaffold level; carried from Wave 5 not-done, now with measured blast radius"}, :event/success 24, :event/done-before 127, :abandoned-parallel-wave {:symptom "19 worktrees at orgs/cloud-itonami/.wave6-* created 09:10-09:17, ~80 min before this wave", :state "each held a written render_html.clj and modified deps.edn, ZERO commits, nothing pushed", :interpretation "an earlier Wave 6 did the work and lost all of it; invisible as a failure because nothing was ever recorded", :action "left untouched (another session uncommitted WIP); agents told not to copy from them", :follow-up "retire or salvage via git-cleanup-conflict; now redundant since all 24 repos landed real renderers"}}
